"""Unselected source decisions; no soul, deity, origin or spell adoption."""
IDS=['alignment-scrying','commune','planar-binding-minor','planar-summons-lesser','planar-summons-greater','soul-cage']
TIERS={
 'alignment-scrying':('B','A location-information effect needs bounded sensing and an evidence-based strong-alignment predicate without inventing a plane taxonomy.'),
 'commune':('C','Actual contact, respondent authority, three answers and hidden cosmology require explicit information and identity boundaries.'),
 'planar-binding-minor':('B','One existing extraplanar target can reuse scoped control/command rules once its CR gate, resistance and finite service are settled.'),
 'planar-summons-lesser':('B','One CR-bounded companion requires a real eligible profile, clear summoning lifecycle and source-specific type selection.'),
 'planar-summons-greater':('C','Two CR8 allies create coupled identity, arrival, control and return questions distinct from the accepted one-ally spell.'),
 'soul-cage':('C','Two source schools disagree on target scope and benefits; capture must preserve Dying/Dead timing, one identity, return blockers and finite soul uses.')
}
Q=[
 ('SC6-Q01',['alignment-scrying'],'Source: spy on a LOCATION where STRONG ALIGNMENT ENERGY exists; Divination5 Action60ft Instantaneous VSF10RP.',
  'A: select one evidenced location with a separately authored strong-energy qualification. B: infer a location from any aligned person or presumed deity/plane name.',
  'Recommend A. Define the actual required location knowledge, maximum destination distance and same/cross-place permissions. Core60ft is preserved evidence and cannot become unlimited by silence. Distinguish casting anchor/range from remote location range only by a declared NEW rule. Actual effective alignment of a creature is not by itself strong location energy. Unknown qualification remains unknown; no search reveals a secret location merely by declaring its desired alignment.'),
 ('SC6-Q02',['alignment-scrying'],'Spy implies information but no sensor, channels, field of view or duration is printed.',
  'A: one instantaneous bounded sensory sample. B: an ongoing mobile sensor requiring a new finite duration and concentration exception.',
  'Prefer A if it preserves useful spying; ask GPT to settle the genuine choice. Specify source point, actual visible/audible channels, three-dimensional sample area, occlusion, illumination, observer viewpoint, perceptible sensor status and detection/countering. Do not grant through-wall vision, translated speech, hidden inventories, exact stats, alignment detection of every occupant or future knowledge. Supply all facts from an authored scene snapshot; a missing scene is a content hold.'),
 ('SC6-Q03',['alignment-scrying'],'Information wards, unknown location qualification and opponent consent cannot be assumed from the spell name.',
  'A: reuse exact accepted information permissions and actual target/ward predicates. B: bypass every ward as alignment magic or grant a new save without source decision.',
  'Specify whether no qualifying site means preflight rejection or paid hidden failure without diagnostic leak; identify any resistance as NEW. Distinguish the location target from creatures incidentally observed. Seal Vision, Nondetection and other actual reviewed counterparts apply only at their own scope; access does not prove cosmic identity. Ordinary Null and suppression timing must be explicit for the sample.'),
 ('SC6-Q04',['commune'],'Ask THREE questions to a DEITY OR POWERFUL ENTITY; Divination5 Action60ft Instantaneous VSF10RP.',
  'A: bounded contact with a real authored eligible respondent. B: an anonymous omniscient answer service or a newly invented patron being.',
  'Recommend A. Define eligibility and how the caster addresses a respondent using an earned channel/known name without requiring hidden true identity. Powerful entity needs a concrete authored qualification, not class level alone. Preserve the deity alternative while respecting that a worship mask/class patron title does not prove an independent being. Unknown respondent authority/contact is a content hold. Choose whether60ft concerns an actual local respondent or a new contact locus; remote reach is an explicit decision, not assumed planar access.'),
 ('SC6-Q05',['commune'],'Three questions have no printed yes/no restriction, word limit, answer guarantee or conversation duration.',
  'A: a finite single resolution with exactly three bounded questions and explicit finite answer forms. B: indefinite conversation or import an external yes/no spell wholesale.',
  'Choose new limits that preserve three meaningful questions. Specify multipart questions, follow-up wording, simultaneous versus ordered answers, language comprehension, refusal/unknown/ambiguous answers and record visibility. Truthful bounded knowledge can be recommended, but truth, cooperation and omniscience are separate rules needing concurrence. A failed contact must not masquerade as a negative answer. No extra Fate presentation or reroll creates knowledge.'),
 ('SC6-Q06',['commune'],'Current owner/reviewed cosmology keeps source facts, mortal theology, respondent knowledge and public revelation separate.',
  'A: answers constrained by actual respondent knowledge and authored scene disclosure. B: automatically reveal Heartcell, Choir/patron equivalences, the Equation, soul jurisdiction or present epoch.',
  'Recommend A with actual authored information, not blanket refusal of useful questions. Ordinary answers may disclose real earned facts. A specific dangerous research/operational revelation uses the reviewed KT/PT/Hunt predicates at actual timing; mere casting or three questions never automatically triggers Hunt. Any voluntary Hunt-capable commitment must receive its real warning before cost; do not retroactively punish an innocuous question. Known access/ward checks and paid hidden failure need explicit ordering.'),
 ('SC6-Q07',['planar-binding-minor'],'Divination6 source compels ONE EXTRAPLANAR creature CR8 or lower to serve; Action60ft Instantaneous VSF13RP.',
  'A: preserve this distinct identity and target predicate. B: alias it to accepted rank5 Planar Binding or infer extraplanar status from creature type.',
  'Recommend A. A current full profile and authoritative CR must support the ceiling; class level, summon rank and HP cannot manufacture CR. Source-explicit extraplanar status can be known while home/native plane remains unknown; discuss exactly what the target needs. Provide sight/line-of-effect, willingness versus hostility, immunities and a NEW resistance save or opposed method. Preserve ordinary Planar Binding as a full comparison only.'),
 ('SC6-Q08',['planar-binding-minor'],'Compelled service has no printed duration, order language, concentration or repeat save.',
  'A: explicit finite service/control with bounded orders and resistance opportunities. B: permanent unrestricted ownership or an instantaneous single command.',
  'Choose and justify a useful NEW completion, preserving original Instantaneous as source conflict. Spell-specific control immunity, communication, one active controller, conflict precedence, prohibited/suicidal orders and damage-trigger/turn-end escape must be explicit. Use actual control and pending-order lifecycle only by an express new extension. Breaking/losing concentration or suppression cannot leave indefinite compulsory service. Ending compulsion need not teleport a pre-existing real creature or erase its independent motives.'),
 ('SC6-Q09',['planar-binding-minor'],'An existing bound creature is not automatically a freshly created summon and cannot gain free actions or another body.',
  'A: complete current-actor state and explicit command/action economy. B: reset HP/resources/life, take ownership of carried gear or add a free companion phase.',
  'Recommend A. Decide existing initiative versus attached phase, limits shared with other owner assets, order delivery/range, default action and command expiry. Track prior summon owner and deadline separately; binding must not refresh an existing creature duration, transfer original damage provenance by implication or duplicate a body. Costs, failure, caster death, lost communication and real release must preserve custody and ordinary agency.'),
 ('SC6-Q10',['planar-summons-lesser'],'Divination5 summons ONE CELESTIAL, ELEMENTAL OR OUTSIDER CR5 or lower; Action60ft Conc60 VSF10RP.',
  'A: a selectable roster of complete current native profiles with independently supported type/CR. B: import an outside stat block or assign CR to an unrated pet.',
  'Recommend A and keep the Divination school/class acquisition. Define outsider using existing native authority or hold that option while preserving its source promise; do not quietly replace it with Fiend. An unrated accepted summon is not an eligible CR5 target simply because its numbers seem similar. Missing profiles remain explicit content holds; a new native profile and rating need separate review. Do not promote old incomplete workbook rows to usable creatures.'),
 ('SC6-Q11',['planar-summons-greater'],'Divination7 summons TWO EXTRAPLANAR ALLIES CR8 or lower EACH; Action120ft Conc60 VSF17RP.',
  'A: two independently qualified complete profiles with distinct instance identities. B: one CR16 budget, one ally, or copy accepted Greater Planar Ally CR6/hour.',
  'Recommend A. Preserve two allies and each ceiling; determine whether exactly two or up-to-two is a new permission. Both must qualify as actual allies and extraplanar independently; shared type/name does not merge their identity. No patron/plane inference from names. Define duplicate roster choice versus duplicate existing individual, partial eligibility/arrival and preflight costs without leaking unknown profile facts.'),
 ('SC6-Q12',['planar-summons-lesser','planar-summons-greater'],'Summon does not resolve whether these are temporary manifestations or transport of independently existing beings.',
  'A: explicitly bounded temporary manifestations with source-qualified profiles. B: real called individuals with complete origin, consent and terminal-return evidence.',
  'Discuss both and choose source-faithfully; neither can be inferred from the school/name. If A, define no duplicate soul/corpse/harvest and distinguish a spell instance from a pre-existing person. If B, require real origin state, absence elsewhere, transport prevention and complete return; do not invent a native plane. Define source-owner/type/healing/Wound/0HP and dispel/suppression lifecycle. No universal Banishment terminal exception is inherited automatically.'),
 ('SC6-Q13',['planar-summons-lesser','planar-summons-greater'],'Both spells require actual body placement, companion commands and finite concentration deadlines.',
  'A: complete supported bodies and exact owner-wide command/offense timing. B: abstract tokens, extra free attacks for each summoned ally or deadline reset through suppression.',
  'Recommend A. Profiles include volume, height, mass, six abilities, defenses, senses, handling, movement, attacks and any equipment/uses. Define range at creation versus command/maintenance, birth/attached phase and legality of ordering either/both bodies under the shared offense ceiling. Clarify innate spells/resources without free refill, actual creationHP feature scope, real cargo/loot, final placement and retained external items. Greater has two distinct arrivals and endings; partial failure must be explicit.'),
 ('SC6-Q14',['soul-cage'],'Enchantment6 traps a DYING CREATURE soul and uses it for various effects; Necromancy6 traps a DYING HUMANOID soul. Both Action60ft Instantaneous VSF13RP.',
  'A: retain school-qualified target scope and explicitly decide which benefits are shared. B: union both source placements and let every class choose the broadest version.',
  'Recommend A. Wizard/Bard/Mirrorsage/Crimson Agent actual access is Enchantment; Cleric/Druid/Shaman is Necromancy. A single catalog identity does not erase these differences. The unrelated Soul Cage feat is comparison only, not a spell procedure or automatic granted benefit. Define proof of an eligible soul without declaring all creatures/types possess or lack souls.'),
 ('SC6-Q15',['soul-cage'],'Source says DYING and casting time Action, not Reaction when a creature dies; current death model distinguishes Dying, Stable, Dead and replacement windows.',
  'A: ordinary Action captures/marks an eligible presently Dying target under an explicit new procedure. B: paid Ready after a real trigger or a new death-window reaction rule.',
  'Preserve the Action. Discuss whether immediate capture can coexist with a living Dying body, or whether a bounded prospective mark captures only at committed death; either is NEW. Do not silently turn dying into dead, make the spell kill the target, block stabilization, bypass a would-die replacement or reach backward after death. Ready setup and its actual reaction release need complete timing, paid resources and target legality. Whole-event Instant Death/Wound and Death Ward versus Ritual of Undeath remain distinct.'),
 ('SC6-Q16',['soul-cage'],'No cage material, custody, duration, capacity, resistance or release terms are printed.',
  'A: one finite nonduplicating custody record with a complete physical or magical container model. B: indefinite portable souls, cloned identities or unbounded stacks.',
  'Choose actual range/sight/LoE, resistance/consent, concentration or nonconcentration deadline, one-soul capacity, holder/owner and transferable custody. If physical, specify complete cage dimensions/mass/AC/HP, mundane versus magical material and actual acquisition/component consumption. If intangible, do not imply free physical cargo. Define suppression/dispel/destruction/caster death/expiry and priority of simultaneous competing cages. All release paths preserve the same identity and history rather than granting resurrection.'),
 ('SC6-Q17',['soul-cage'],'Enchantment promises various uses but neither source lists a menu, amounts or use counts.',
  'A: a small fully enumerated new menu with finite charges and action costs. B: import another game menu, arbitrary wishes or deny all use while calling the spell complete.',
  'Require GPT to propose the smallest source-faithful complete menu and flag every new effect for exact follow-up. For any knowledge mode, actual memory/language/revelation limits apply. For healing/resource modes, define legitimate recipients, real HP/RP caps, once-only consumption and ordinary anti-refund rules. No automatic new soul destruction, torture benefit, inherited skill/class feature, unlimited energy or learned Equation is granted. Decide if Necromancy gains this menu only through explicit sourced/new extension, otherwise preserve distinct modes.'),
 ('SC6-Q18',['soul-cage'],'Current reviewed soul rules preserve one continuing identity, committed-death history, Hunted Death and uniquely consumed rare intervention.',
  'A: spell custody and return eligibility remain separate records. B: cage bypasses Hunt, erases death, creates a spare soul or becomes an ordinary Divine/Abyssal intervention.',
  'Recommend A. Determine whether actual capture creates a narrowly defined return blocker and what release removes; never infer pending Resurrection/Clone efficacy. An actual independently authored intervention must explicitly override the relevant blocker and settle body, HP, Wounds, inventory, location and obligations. Returning an alive Dying target, reviving a dead identity and releasing custody are different operations. Actual resurrection/cage conflicts need a named rule, not lore inference.'),
 ('SC6-Q19',['alignment-scrying','commune','planar-binding-minor','planar-summons-lesser','planar-summons-greater','soul-cage'],'The prior source questions postponed cosmology-linked work until the preservation push; that push is now independently verified.',
  'A: discuss finite spell mechanics with complete original manuscripts, saved website and owner qualifications. B: treat the push as adoption of the mortal Wheel, website topology, planar clock conversion or a soul/deity identity.',
  'Recommend A. Keep original source evidence, mortal beliefs, current scoped mechanics and unresolved owner choices separate. Neither helper plane keys nor a functioning class/spell proves hidden ontology. No missing World I–VI, Equation content, Serit bridge, Maladomini ruler, Heartcell builder or campaign epoch may be invented. Genuine setting-content dependencies are explicit holds, not fabricated defaults or a reason to erase the printed spell.'),
 ('SC6-Q20',['alignment-scrying','commune','planar-binding-minor','planar-summons-lesser','planar-summons-greater','soul-cage'],'No earlier complete procedures or operational scenarios exist for these six identities; original question records must remain unchanged.',
  'A: resolve each real question, then author complete legal current cases and seek exact acceptance. B: promote a source packet, conditional snippet, passing file check or consent to discuss into completed review.',
  'Recommend A. Each later case needs real accessible caster/class level, RP and all used counters, school-specific acquisition, V/S/F, finite time and actual body/source state. Preserve all original source/questions; at least two full cases per identity plus every distinct school/form/profile/return branch. Missing eligible creature/scene/respondent/soul evidence remains a whole-case hold. No blanket C risk, deletion, runtime/human/balance/cosmology or whole-domain closure.')
]
